    "intro_html":  "Chicken Marbella made its name in the early eighties as the dinner party dish that could be made entirely ahead, and forty years later that is exactly why it belongs in a meal prep rotation. Chicken marinates overnight in red wine vinegar, oregano, garlic, olives, and dried fruit, then roasts in the same pan with brown sugar on top. It is salty, sweet, and sour at once, and it gets better every day it sits. Each serving lands at 566 calories and \u003cstrong\u003e41 grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e$3.82 a serving\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost).",
